Exactly.  This helps in a lot of ways.

> Can this be done directly in the model or peak_Ft this now a transformed parameter? I also assume I only have to do this for the first time since peak_Ft[t] is a function of the previous time point.

That would work the same way, by breaking down the normal

  foo[t] ~ normal(g(foo[t-1]), sigma);

as

  foo_raw[t] ~ normal(0, 1);

  foo[t] = g(foo[t - 1]) + sigma * foo_raw[t];

where g is any kind of function you want.

