If you want, you can also preview the makeover coming to some of our plots by trying out the in-development bayesplot package here <http://github.com/jgabry/bayesplot> (will be moved to stan-dev soon). The version of the plot you're making would be this (using one of the Stan demo models as an example):

devtools::install_github("jgabry/bayesplot") # temporary home

library("rstan")
library("bayesplot")

fit <- stan_demo("eight_schools")
x <- as.matrix(fit, pars = "theta")

mcmc_intervals(x)

mcmc_intervals(x) +
    ylab("Parameters") +
    coord_flip() +
    theme_default(x_lab = TRUE, y_lab = FALSE)

Changing the parameter labels will also be much easier, as you can just change any of the column names of the x matrix instead of having to mess with the ggplot object.

Jonah

