So I have done my best to implement all of your suggestions, however I keep getting the error:
Exception thrown at line 215: normal_log: Location parameter[2236] is -nan, but must be finite!
If this warning occurs sporadically, such as for highly constrained variable types like covariance matrices, then the sampler is fine,
but if this warning occurs often then your model may be either severely ill-conditioned or misspecified.
without any convergence. Before, I'd get this a few times and then it would converge.

Here is the updated code:
functions {
    //Compute the k parameter
    real get_k(real Ft, real Bt){
        return (sqrt(Ft^2*(4*Bt+Ft^2))+2*Bt+Ft^2)/(2*Bt);
    }

    //Compute the theta parameter
    real get_theta(real Ft, real Bt){
        return (sqrt(Ft^2*(4*Bt+Ft^2))-Ft^2)/(2*Ft);
    }

    //Compute the fixed term in the gamma function
    real get_gamma_term(real At, real k, real theta){
        return At/(exp(1-k)*((k-1)*theta)^(k-1));
    }

    //Compute the gamma function
    real gamma(real gamma_term, real k, real theta, real freq){
        return gamma_term*freq^(k-1)*exp(-freq/theta);
    }
}

data {
    int<lower=0>         Nt; //number of times
