Below is an example where there is a geom_line() linking up data points for each subject over time and separate panel for each level of a factor (in this case cognitive classification, in your case would be number of electrodes). To get this you'd add '+facet_wrap(~n_electrodes)' to your plot.

 <https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-DmHkI_ipOTE/V_Vagw35VMI/AAAAAAAAAKI/MmxmVfbBuX0xJxUxfLc8QvaSx0w_ow_BgCEw/s1600/Screenshot%2B2016-10-06%2B08.54.10.png>

In this case the group-level predictor of cognitive group has a strong effect on the intercept and a modest effect on the slope.

I appreciate how difficult it is collecting this type of data. You'll still be able to fit a model that will give useful results, although the choice of priors and model structure become more important.

Regards,

Daniel

