Hi Daniel,

first of all thanks for all the suggestions. So I have tried both, using indexed gamma values for every of the five electrode counts (as Bob suggested) and I have also tried multiplying gamma with the number of electrodes. Results were both similar. But what actually changed a lot was using multivariate priors for intercept and slope (all according to chapter 6.12 in the manual) and especially when I restricted the group-level interaction to the slope (see the attached model). This is the output:

