Regarding your finding: In the case we just examined, the lack of direct equivalence between the iterative and vectorized forms suggests that the vectorized form of the statement is doing the equivalent of the pass-by-value of the entire vector block (or nonsequental pass-by-reference) at the moment of first execution. Is that correct? That makes it the same as most languages, and makes a great deal of sense.

