I have been getting the same error on long runs on the same computer. The last time I was running 3 chains and I only got it on one node. Two of the three finished after 250,000 seconds but the third took 868,500 seconds. Before I have gotten it on more than one node. It looks like it indeed has something to do with files disappearing after a long run time. If open_progress = FALSE will solve this I will try it. But I don't know what that does.

On Wednesday, September 28, 2016 at 10:38:43 AM UTC-4, H. X. wrote:

> Hi All,
> After finishing sampling, I got the error message:
>  Elapsed Time: 757694 seconds (Warm-up)
>                930398 seconds (Sampling)
>                1.68809e+06 seconds (Total)
>
> Error in file(file, "r") : cannot open the connection
> Calls: stan -> sampling -> sampling -> .local -> scan -> file
> In addition: Warning message:
> In file(file, "r") :
>   cannot open file '/var/folders/15/2v3s52zj6px1zmw2y17vvtpr0000gp/T//Rtmp1QXevN/file8506f3e5a4b': No such file or directory
> Execution halted
>
