I wanted to inquire whether Stan has functionality for Bayesian Optimization, as a tool for automatic model & parameter selection. (as described in this paper <http://ieeexplore.ieee.org/document/7352306/>) . There are software tools for this in python, Java & C++. However, when I searched for any existing R packages, I found this one: rBayesianOptimization  <https://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/rBayesianOptimization/rBayesianOptimization.pdf)>(https://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/rBayesianOptimization/rBayesianOptimization.pdf). It cites Prof. Adam's paper from <https://arxiv.org/abs/1206.2944> Harvard (https://arxiv.org/abs/1206.2944)

Thanks,
-- Daniel

