Hi Wally and Gary,

Perhaps the most prudent thing to do is to run through CmdStan if there are things happening out of your control. It streams output to a file and there's nothing else written out to any temp space. You should get the same results with the same seeds on the same architecture, compiler, etc. (and you probably won't get the same results if you use different architectures or compiler settings).

Daniel

