Hi

I had posted a few days back about doing a Discrete Choice analysis using Stan as Hierarchical Bayes model. One of the forum members, Daniel (thank you again!) had pointed me to an awesome article by Akiva, McFadden, and Train (link http://eml.berkeley.edu/~train/foundations.pdf ). The paper goes in depth into current state of affairs in stated preference methods and the authors compare different approaches in analyzing a synthetic data set. The appendix (pages 112 - 117) has complete documentation for

1. Setting up the *.stan file
2. Setting up the *.R file (I'm using RStan)
3. Creating the synthetic data set in R

I modified the ".stan and .R" files from this paper for a choice data set I had with 1068 respondents. The R output below (warnings and errors) is what I got when I ran the model with either 1068 or 30 respondents. I reran the model with 30 respondents so I could get the output quickly. To keep the post to reasonable length, I'm going to upload my stan, R, and csv data files as well. If one of you could help me identify how I can correct the errors, it would be very helpful

