You want to make sure your R-hat values are all near 1
and you have n_eff large enough for your inferential
needs.

Yes, 0.8 is OK.  It's our default and the target we're
trying to adapt to.  But it's ***not*** a Metropolis
acceptance rate.

If anything, we often need to raise adapt_delta above 0.8 for
more complicated posteriors.

- Bob

