No, if it's still stuck on iteration 1 it's going to remain
stuck.  It's probably a big model with challenging curvature
and inits out in the tails, which can cause the step size to
get very low and the number of steps get very high and essentially
look like it's frozen.

I'd run many fewer iterations than 20K, though, unless you need a huge
n_eff for some reason.

- Bob

