Ok sounds good. I understand your point that it's difficult to determine convergence given a single path and log density - my suggestion was not to determine convergence, more to amend this as a first variable length initialization stage, and to move on to 'regular initialisation / warmup' after a few iterations where the log density is no longer increasing. But I'm happy if you have bigger and better plans for this sort of problem. In the meantime when this is a problem I've decided to optimize, with hyper variances fixed at a medium to high values, to determine start values... something that will probably induce head shaking from a few but is working well in these cases.

