Thanks Bob for getting back.

1. As I learn more about Stan ( and RStan & CmdStan) I'm seeing that how I set up RStan for comparison will be critical.
2. I finally got to read your presentation slides (the Vanderbilt slides) that compares MH, Gibbs, HMC with the NUT sampler and I see that Stan with NUT sampler is a lot more efficient than the MH and Gibbs. Other forum members too have advised me that my 20,000 iterations is an overkill.
