So RTools 3.4 doesn't work with Windows 10 Home Premium with Anniversary Update? And what does that mean? Is g++ on the path? Is everything you need on the path? can you call all of that from the command line directly? Does it conflict with the internal bash tools that the Anniversary Update gives you?

>
> The uname message pops up with Windows 10 and not Windows 7. I will be running more tests and I will document here.

The uname message appears when there's no uname on the path. I haven't figured out how to suppress it from the makefile and I've given it a few hours of time, so I don't think it's something I will be able to find. I'm sure there's some way to suppress it safely, but it's one of those things where you'll know how to find the solution if you already know the solution and it's very hard to stumble into the solution online.

It's just a message, so please ignore it.

Daniel

