Another old post that nobody responded to.

The problem is that your scale's not identified in the likelihood
only in the weak prior on tau_k.

>   real<lower = 0> tau_k;
>

>   real<lower = 0> tau_i[n_respondents];

>   tau_i ~ normal(1, tau_i_sigma);

>   tau_k ~ normal(0, 5);

>       z[m] ~ normal(alpha[i[m]] + beta[i[m]] * theta[i[m]], tau_k * tau_i[i[m]]);

I'm guessing you'll see banana-shaped pairs plots in
the posterior of tau_k * tau_i.

This could also be vectorized for a bit more efficiency if you
could presort the conditional in the actual code out.

I'm afraid I don't have a suggestion for how to fix this.

- Bob

