I don't understand (I might be dense):
x ∼ normal(0, 1) ⇒ ∀t ∈ R, Pr(x ≥ t) > 0.
x ≡ simplex[3] ⇒ ∀t > 1, Pr(x[1] > t) = 0. (And, BTW, x ≡ simplex[3] ⇒ ∀t < 0, Pr(x[1] < t) = 0.)
Those two constraints are simply incompatible... And I have trouble understanding what Stan makes of these statements.

Care to explain ?

--
